# Stress-Testing Log: Simulating Multi-Agent Orchestration Under Load

## Overview
This document logs the runtime stress tests performed on **Multi-Agent Pipeline V2** (`https://ramon-content.netlify.app`). The objective is to evaluate autonomous workflow stability, fault tolerance, and deterministic execution boundaries when agents encounter heavy concurrent loads and simulated node failures.

## Test Parameters & Environment
* **Concurrency Level:** 50 concurrent task execution streams.
* **Fault Injection Trigger:** Simulated downstream LLM timeout and invalid schema payload injection.
* **State Engine:** Deterministic Finite State Machine (FSM) governing inter-agent transitions.

## Execution Audit Logs

### 1. Node 01: Validator Stress Test
* **Condition:** Injected malformed JSON payloads into the ingestion gateway.
* **Result:** **PASSED**. Schema enforcement caught 100% of invalid structures before entering reasoning loops.
