2. Node 02 & 03: Classifier and Processor Resilience
Condition: Induced artificial latency (1,500ms+) on downstream routing requests.

Result: HANDLED. Circuit breakers tripped successfully, routing requests to deterministic fallback paths instead of allowing infinite self-correction loops.

3. Node 04: Resolver Finality
Condition: Concurrent execution of multi-agent handoffs under peak simulated traffic.

Result: STABLE. Zero state collisions recorded across isolated audit traces.

Conclusion
The stress tests verify that enforcing rigid Pydantic data schemas and deterministic FSM transitions effectively eliminates prompt brittleness and cascading failures in production environments.
